# Android release signing. Copy to `keystore.properties` (git-ignored) and fill in.
#
# Read at build time by plugins/withReleaseSigning.js. Without all four values, and without the
# SILENTSUM_KEYSTORE_* environment variables below, any release build STOPS -- it does not fall
# back to the debug key, because Play rejects debug-signed uploads and `debug.keystore` is the
# same key in every React Native checkout.
#
# This file lives in the project root, not in android/: `expo prebuild` deletes android/ whole.
#
# storeFile may be absolute, or relative to this directory. Keep the keystore OUTSIDE the
# repository if you can; `*.jks` and `*.keystore` are git-ignored either way.
#
# Back the keystore up somewhere you will still have in five years. Play will not accept an app
# signed with a replacement key, and there is no recovery path except Play App Signing key reset,
# which needs a working upload key to request.

storeFile=
storePassword=
keyAlias=
keyPassword=

# Alternatively, for CI that holds these as secrets, leave this file absent and set:
#   SILENTSUM_KEYSTORE_FILE
#   SILENTSUM_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
#   SILENTSUM_KEY_ALIAS
#   SILENTSUM_KEY_PASSWORD
